417] [17592186425056 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425056 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $A$ be a $7\\times 12$ matrix that has $6$ **pivot** columns. What is the rank of the matrix?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425056 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6826463c-847d-5512-b760-3fbeb596f635" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425056 #edb/ref 1074 "We know that $\\text{rank}(A)$ is the number of pivot columns in $A.$ \n\nSince we are told that $A$ has $6$ pivot columns, we have \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)=6.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425057 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425052 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425057 #edb/ref 1069 "q-35285" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425057 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425057 #edb/ref 1071 "If \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -9 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}]$, then $\\text{rank}(A)=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425057 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6e4ed9e5-eccc-52bc-8945-b31db9b251e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425057 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the rank of $A,$ we first reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -9 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $2$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $2$ non-zero rows).\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(A)=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425058 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425058 #edb/ref 1069 "q-79560" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425058 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425058 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following matrices has a rank of $3?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425058 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8c046845-0154-54e8-9266-c14fc31a0fbc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425058 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that a matrix of rank $3$ must have at least $3$ columns and at least $3$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the following matrices:\n\n- $A$ since it has only $2$ rows.\n\n- $B$ since it has only $2$ rows (and only $2$ columns).\n\n- $E$ since it has only $2$ columns.\n\nAlso, the matrix must have $3$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $C$ has exactly $3$ pivot columns, while the matrix $D$ has only $2$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(C)=3$ and $\\text{rank}(D)=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the matrix $C.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425061 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425061 #edb/ref 1069 "q-79157" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425061 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425061 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $B$ be a $4\\times 5$ matrix that has $3$ **pivot** columns. What is the rank of the matrix?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425061 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d99c604a-a10b-57d3-8148-d6702b5326c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425061 #edb/ref 1074 "We know that $\\text{rank}(B)$ is the number of pivot columns in $B.$ \n\nSince we are told that $B$ has $3$ pivot columns, we have \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(B)=3.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425062 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425053 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425062 #edb/ref 1069 "q-79405" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425062 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425062 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $A$ be a $8\\times 9$ matrix that has $4$ **pivot** columns. What is the rank of the matrix?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425062 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e56cf627-f5bb-57b0-ae99-521a4ce7bf5a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425062 #edb/ref 1074 "We know that $\\text{rank}(A)$ is the number of pivot columns in $A.$ \n\nSince we are told that $A$ has $4$